# Low-Cost Index Funds

The core investment vehicle recommended by the Index Card Rules framework. Broad-market index funds offer instant diversification, minimal fees, and consistent long-term performance that exceeds most actively managed funds.

## Why Index Funds Win

- **Instant diversification** — owning hundreds or thousands of companies
- **Low fees** — 0.03-0.04% expense ratios vs 1%+ for active funds
- **Outperform most professionals** — over long time horizons
- **No stock picking required** — set and forget

## Example Funds

- **VTSAX** — Vanguard Total Stock Market (0.04%)
- **VFIAX** — Vanguard S&P 500 (0.04%)
- **FXAIX** — Fidelity S&P 500 (0.015%)
- **SWTSX** — Schwab Total Stock Market (0.03%)
- **VTTHX** — Vanguard 2055 Target Date (auto-adjusts allocation by age)

## The Math of Fees

- 0.04% fee: keep 99.96% of returns
- 1% fee: keep 99% of returns
- Over 30 years, a 1% fee costs 25%+ of your final balance

